# Nekobi for WebCLAP

Nekobi by DISTRHO (a TB-303-style bass synthesizer, based on Nekobee by Sean Bolton and others), ported to WebCLAP. This is not an official DISTRHO release.

- Nekobi: https://github.com/DISTRHO/Nekobi (commit 276f0c4, GPL-2.0-or-later)
- [DPF](https://github.com/DISTRHO/DPF) (commit 4238e1c), the DISTRHO Plugin Framework the plugin is written with
- This port, and the complete source of this bundle: @SOURCE_URL@
  Build it with `scripts/build-nekobi.sh`, which fetches every dependency below at the commit named here.

## License

The bundle as a whole is licensed under the **GNU General Public License, version 2 or later** (`LICENSE`) (`LICENSE`).

Nekobi is GPL-2.0-or-later, based on Nekobee by Sean Bolton and others (`licenses/Nekobi-GPL-2.0.txt`). DPF is ISC
(`licenses/DPF-ISC.txt`), which is compatible with the GPL; `module.wasm` as a whole is GPL-2.0-or-later. The bundle's
`LICENSE` is the GPL-2.0.

This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied
warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the licenses for details.

The bundle holds the DSP only (`module.wasm`): DPF's own CLAP wrapper compiled to WebAssembly. The plugin's graphical
editor is not part of it, hosts show the plugin's parameters instead.

